Shim speed patch for Rowan (frozen files: NOT applied).   git apply Testing/notes/shim_speed.patch
REBASED 2026-11-03 onto festive-fermi 5845b97 (after proof/fastq-failfast and proof/trimrecord). Touches Spec/Fastq.lean, Spec/Sam.lean, their copies
Proofs/Fastq.lean, Proofs/Sam.lean, and Proofs/TrimRecord.lean + Testing/scripts/CI_check.sh (the proofs and axiom list follow the field type change).
Order: independent of audit_medium_patches/shim_fasta_failfast.patch (applies before or after it). Measurements below are from 562a2f5.

Items, measured cumulatively at 562a2f5 (callgrind Ir of the shim, first 2000 pairs, index load included; base
NovaSeq 985.5M, HiSeq hg002 2x250 1359.0M). SAM byte-identical to base at every step on both subsets; with all four
items, also identical on the four full 200k sets (NovaSeq, mason, low, HiSeq), and CI_check.sh passes.
| step | change | NovaSeq | HiSeq |
| 1 | reverseMapBytes @[specialize]: f (complementByte / id) was a closure call per byte | -32.1M (-3.3%) | -49.1M (-3.6%) |
| 2 | samName / mateName: (name.takeWhile (· != ' ')).toString instead of (name.splitOn " ").headD _ | -29.3M (-3.0%) | -20.3M (-1.5%) |
| 3 | findNewline: USize loop with uget (findNewlineU), the while loop kept as the fallback | -14.4M (-1.5%) | -21.7M (-1.6%) |
| 4 | FastqRecord.quality : ByteArray (was String): no UTF-8 round trips when reading / trimming; SAM QUAL decoded once | -26.0M (-2.6%) | -40.3M (-3.0%) |
| all | | 883.8M (-10.3%) | 1227.6M (-9.7%) |
Notes:
- Step 2 gives the same string: the part before the first space (splitOn with a non-empty separator always has a
  first piece; with no space it is the whole name).
- Step 3's findNewlineU is not proved equal to the while loop (needs a lemma if the file must stay proof-equal);
  it returns the same index on the four full sets.
- Step 4 changes a Spec structure's field type (FastqRecord.quality); trimRecord now hands the quality bytes to
  AdapterTrim.cutTruSeq / ReadTrim.trimRead directly. Nothing else in Spec/, Main.lean or the proofs reads the
  field. The SAM text is unchanged.

Rebase notes (what changed against the 562a2f5 version):
- parseRecord (fail-fast reader) now builds `quality` as the checked ByteArray (no String round trip); readChunk compares letters.size with quality.size.
- Proofs/TrimRecord.lean: trimBytes takes record.quality directly; trimRecord_correct also states the quality window on the record;
  trimRecord_quality_bytes / fromUTF8!_toUTF8 are gone (the field is bytes); parseRecord_trim_quality now says (trimRecord record).quality is valid UTF-8
  for every record parseRecord returns, i.e. the SAM's String.fromUTF8! on QUAL (forward strand) cannot panic. Reverse strand reads them reversed: not proved.
  CI_check.sh requires the new axiom list (trimRecord_quality_bytes removed).
- Re-verified at the rebase: CI_check.sh and FUZZ=1 pass; SAM byte-identical to the unpatched binary on the fuzz set and on the first 20k NovaSeq pairs
  (40000 records).

